    "collapsible-content": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible-row-3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "List of ingredients",
            "icon": "leaf",
            "row_content": "<p>Glycerin, Propylene Glycol, Deionized Water, Sodium Phytate, Carbomer, Carboxymethyl, Polyvinylpyrrolidone, Menthol<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible-row-1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Instructions",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>1. <\/strong>Ensure your teeth are dry before using.<br\/><br\/><strong>2.<\/strong> Peel off the long strip and apply sticky side to the top half of your teeth.<br\/><br\/><strong>3.<\/strong> Press strip down firmly and folder over the back of your teeth to secure.<br\/><br\/><strong>4.<\/strong> Repeat the same for the bottom half with the shorter strip.<br\/><br\/><strong>5. <\/strong>Leave on your teeth for 30 minutes for maximum whitening treatment.<br\/><br\/><strong>6.<\/strong> Remove strips and rinse mouth with water.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible-row-0": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Warnings",
            "icon": "lightning_bolt",
            "row_content": "<ul><li>Avoid using strips after brushing your teeth. Allow at least one hour after brushing teeth before using the strips.<br\/><\/li><li>Do not re-use the strips, dispose of the strips once used.<br\/><\/li><li>The ingredients of the strips are safe and if some gel is swallowed it is perfectly safe.<br\/><\/li><li>Clean off any remaining gel residue by gargling with warm water.<br\/><\/li><li>If strip is difficult to remove from your teeth, simply lubricate the strip with water and remove.<br\/><\/li><li>Regularly use whitening strips every three months to obtain a whiter, brighter smile.<\/li><\/ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "dc156c5a-46c9-43e5-acbd-475340353fc0": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do teeth whitening strips whiten?",
            "icon": "eye",
            "row_content": "<p>When applied to your teeth, each strip firmly adheres to the tooth surface and releases the active ingredients of the whitening formula into the tooth’s structure to help lift surface stains while remaining gentle on teeth<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "1efe8090-8cc3-4d87-874c-e2af1cea652a": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Whats in the box?",
            "icon": "box",
            "row_content": "<p>Each order of teeth whitening strips consists of 14 treatments.<br\/><br\/><strong>14x<\/strong> individually packed strips for individual uses.<br\/><br\/><strong>1x<\/strong> Teeth shade chart (to monitor and track your progress)<br\/><br\/><strong>1x <\/strong>Manual<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wPUNyh": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can the Teeth Whitening Strips be used on composite bonding, veneers or fillings?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, it can be used on composite bonding, veneers, and fillings. While it will not whiten these materials, it effectively helps to remove daily stains.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
